{
  "company_name": "BuildBid Engineering",
  "industry": "Construction & Engineering",
  "use_case": "Engineering bid creation and cost estimation analytics",
  "space_title": "BuildBid Engineering - Bid Creation & Cost Estimation 📝",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Construction & Engineering\n\n**Use case:** Engineering Bid Creation & Cost Estimation\n\nBuildBid Engineering — EPC bid analytics across 20 active pursuits in bridges, highways, commercial, water, tunnels, industrial, and energy. Estimating Leads and Cost Engineers use this space to triangulate labor/material/equipment build-ups and competitive markup; VP Construction and the CFO use it to track win rate, pipeline coverage, and estimate accuracy against booked margin.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Bid win rate (%) — industry benchmark 20-35% on hard-bid public work, 40-60% on negotiated\n- Estimate accuracy (%) — target >90% vs. as-built (AACE Class 2 estimates)\n- Bid markup / target margin (%) — typical 8-15% on competitive lump-sum work\n- Average competitors per bid — directional pricing pressure indicator\n- Pipeline coverage ($) — target 3-4x trailing annual revenue\n- Cost mix (labor/material/equipment/subcontractor) — used for risk-loaded contingency\n- Contingency (%) — typical 3-10% depending on design maturity\n- Total bid value submitted ($) — top-of-funnel volume\n\n**Data sources**\n- `projects` — daily bid submissions: estimated cost, bid amount, target margin, result (Won/Lost/Pending/Withdrawn)\n- `bid_submissions` — weekly cost estimate snapshots with labor, material, equipment, subcontractor build-up and contingency\n- `cost_estimate_snapshots` — monthly bid-performance roll-ups: bids submitted/won, pipeline value, estimate accuracy, competitor count",
  "schema_basename": "ce_bid_creation",
