  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports the bid-creation function at an EPC contractor — Estimating Leads, Cost Engineers, the VP of Construction, and the CFO collaborate here to build, price, and review proposals across bridges, highways, commercial buildings, water/wastewater, tunnels, industrial, and energy work. Bid economics are driven by labor productivity, material indices, equipment time on site, subcontractor coverage, contingency, and target margin. Pipeline coverage and win rate by project_type and region steer go/no-go decisions.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Bid win rate = won_count / bid_count; industry benchmark 20-35% hard-bid, 40-60% negotiated.\n- Estimate accuracy = estimate_accuracy_pct on cost_estimate_snapshots; AACE Class 2 target >90%.\n- Bid markup / target margin = target_margin_pct on projects; typical 8-15% on competitive lump-sum.\n- Total direct cost = labor_cost_usd + material_cost_usd + equipment_cost_usd + subcontractor_cost_usd from bid_submissions.\n- Contingency = contingency_pct on bid_submissions; typical 3-10% depending on design maturity.\n- Pipeline value = pipeline_value_usd on cost_estimate_snapshots; target coverage 3-4x trailing annual revenue.\n- Competitive intensity = avg_competitors on cost_estimate_snapshots; >5 suggests commoditized lane.\n- Bid volume = SUM(bid_amount_usd) — top-of-funnel pursuit dollars.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - bid_kpi_monthly (source: projects) — dims: bid_date, project_type, region, bid_result; measures: total_bid_amount, total_estimated_cost, avg_target_margin, bid_count, won_count, unique_project_count, max_estimated_cost.\n  - pipeline_kpi_monthly (source: cost_estimate_snapshots) — dims: perf_month, project_type, region; measures: total_bids_submitted, total_bids_won, total_pipeline, avg_estimate_accuracy, avg_competitors, unique_project_count, max_bids_submitted.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. project_id, project_name, labor_cost_usd, material_cost_usd, contingency_pct).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly bid win count and total bid value trended over the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 project types by win rate this year — and how does that compare to average target margin?",
    "Which regions have the lowest estimate accuracy over the last 6 months, and what's the total pipeline value at risk?",
    "How has average competitors per bid trended monthly across the network?",
    "Top 10 projects by total bid value submitted this year, with bid result and target margin.",
    "What is the monthly trend in total pipeline value by project type for the trailing 12 months?",
    "Which project types have the highest average contingency percentage, and how does that correlate with win rate?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique projects?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT bid_date, MEASURE(unique_project_count) AS unique_project_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.bid_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY bid_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest estimated cost changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT bid_date, MEASURE(max_estimated_cost) AS max_estimated_cost",
        "FROM {fqn}.bid_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY bid_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has avg competitors per bid changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, MEASURE(avg_competitors) AS avg_competitors",
        "FROM {fqn}.pipeline_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total estimated project cost usd over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT bid_date, SUM(estimated_cost_usd) AS total_estimated_cost_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.projects",
        "GROUP BY bid_date ORDER BY bid_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total labor cost usd over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT estimate_date, SUM(labor_cost_usd) AS total_labor_cost_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.bid_submissions",
        "GROUP BY estimate_date ORDER BY estimate_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average cost estimate accuracy 0-100 changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, AVG(estimate_accuracy_pct) AS avg_estimate_accuracy_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.cost_estimate_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY perf_month ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has won count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT bid_date, MEASURE(won_count) AS won_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.bid_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY bid_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
